# Wan Shi Tong, Librarian: "Whenever AN opponent searches their library" - in a three-player game both of Bot1's opponents count. Bot2 cracks
# an Arid Mesa on turn 2 and Bot3 on turn 3, each finding a Plains: Wan Shi Tong gets a counter and Bot1 draws a card for each,
# two in all (a 3/3 and two more cards; Bot1 drew on turn 1 as the first player of a three-player game, CR 103.8a).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Wan Shi Tong, Librarian
Island x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Arid Mesa
Plains x6
Mountain
Plains x10

[Bot3 Deck]
Arid Mesa
Plains x6
Mountain
Plains x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Wan Shi Tong, Librarian.Cast(X: 0)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Arid Mesa.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Arid Mesa.Activate
Bot2.Search(Plains)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Wan Shi Tong, Librarian.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
[T3 Bot3.Main1]
Bot3.Hand.Arid Mesa.Play
Bot3.Battlefield.Arid Mesa.Activate
Bot3.Search(Plains)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
[T3 Bot3.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Wan Shi Tong, Librarian.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Wan Shi Tong, Librarian.Power = 3
Bot1.Hand.Count = 7
